WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.160
Gary W. Goldstein, Producer/Author/Instructor:
I’m not going to share who I am as an artist,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:02.160 --> 00:00:08.400
as a creator, as a writer. I’m going to put out a&nbsp;
blind query letter with a log line, etc and I’ll&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:15.920
send it to a stranger who does not yet know me and&nbsp;
I’m going to hope and pray to get a good response.

00:00:15.920 --> 00:00:18.840
Film Courage: Is Hollywood a game, Gary?

00:00:18.840 --> 00:00:26.240
Gary: In a sense yes I suppose but I think&nbsp;
life in a way is a game in the best sense.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:36.000
But you sort of have to understand the rules of&nbsp;
it. People talk about ‘breaking into Hollywood,’&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:46.400
which I always find fascinating because life is&nbsp;
not an event, it's a process right and I think&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:55.520
when people think about…people are very given&nbsp;
to stories in their craft and their dream of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.520 --> 00:01:01.440
what it is they want to accomplish we know at&nbsp;
show business. But very few people really think&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:07.440
about the business side of the equation and&nbsp;
I find a lot of creatives in particular are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:14.080
not intentionally random but they end&nbsp;
up being random in their approach,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:17.520
focusing on craft not thinking&nbsp;
about how they're going to navigate.

00:01:20.800 --> 00:01:28.800
As if our industry is somehow different from&nbsp;
all other industries which it's not I mean&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:37.520
it is in a sense but it's not in the sense of&nbsp;
being relationship based um and I you know what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.520 --> 00:01:43.440
what I would encourage people is I try and train&nbsp;
people to be hyper focused hyper intentional&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.720 --> 00:01:52.560
radically transparent and not think about needing&nbsp;
a representative so much as being themselves a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.560 --> 00:01:59.120
presence developing rapport creating relationships&nbsp;
in this business and understanding that the first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.120 --> 00:02:04.560
thing they have to know is who are you who are&nbsp;
you in the world what do you care about what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.280 --> 00:02:09.840
what's your creative DNA what's your signature&nbsp;
what what are the kinds of stories you want to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.840 --> 00:02:13.600
participating in or writing or directing&nbsp;
or producing whatever it might be&nbsp;&nbsp;

